.TH mouser-mcp-servers-add 1  "mouser-mcp-servers-add 1.4.4" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-mcp\-servers\-add \- Add or update: `add NAME \-\-url URL [\-\-token\-stdin] [\-\-ca PEM]` or `add NAME \-\- COMMAND ARGS…`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser mcp servers add\fR [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\fR] [\fB\-\-env\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add or update: `add NAME \-\-url URL [\-\-token\-stdin] [\-\-ca PEM]` or `add NAME \-\- COMMAND ARGS…`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-token\-stdin\fR
Read a bearer token from stdin (stored in the OS keychain, never in preferences)
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\fR \fI<CA>\fR
PEM certificate/CA to trust for an https URL
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Environment for a stdio server, K=V (V may be keychain:NAME); repeatable
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
